From: radiance-web EnergyPlus WASM port
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] third_party/fmt-8.0.1: de-space user-defined-literal operators (xchar.h)

What: `operator"" _format` -> `operator""_format` and `operator"" _a` -> `operator""_a`
in xchar.h (the wchar_t overloads; format.h's char overloads are patch 0002).

Why (toolchain, not physics): same clang>=23 deprecated-literal-operator
promotion as patch 0002 -- tokenization-only, no behavior change.

Applies to: energyplus-src/third_party/fmt-8.0.1/include/fmt/xchar.h
Apply with (-p1, from the pristine energyplus-src/ tree root):
  patch -p1 < patches/energyplus/0003-fmt8-udl-xchar-h.patch

--- a/third_party/fmt-8.0.1/include/fmt/xchar.h
+++ b/third_party/fmt-8.0.1/include/fmt/xchar.h
@@ -47,13 +47,13 @@
 }
 
 inline namespace literals {
-constexpr auto operator"" _format(const wchar_t* s, size_t n)
+constexpr auto operator""_format(const wchar_t* s, size_t n)
     -> detail::udl_formatter<wchar_t> {
   return {{s, n}};
 }
 
 #if FMT_USE_USER_DEFINED_LITERALS && !FMT_USE_NONTYPE_TEMPLATE_PARAMETERS
-constexpr detail::udl_arg<wchar_t> operator"" _a(const wchar_t* s, size_t) {
+constexpr detail::udl_arg<wchar_t> operator""_a(const wchar_t* s, size_t) {
   return {s};
 }
 #endif
